    "interpretation": "Validation accept rate (0.571) exactly equals raw accuracy (0.571) -- this is not a coincidence, it is mathematically forced: for a single-fault FaultLine instance, patching module X restores success if and only if X is the true fault module (that IS the ground-truth construction, Step 2.4). So validation accepts iff the reflection already guessed correctly. Precision when it accepts is 1.000 -- also forced by the same logic, not a discovery. The honest characterization of RCA here: reflection+validation gives a 100%-precision CONFIRMED answer 57.1% of the time, and abstains (uniform, no informative credit) the other 42.9% -- not a 71.4%-accurate classifier. This is a precision/coverage tradeoff finding, not an accuracy number, and should be written up as such."
